  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $\u03a6(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X\u223cN(-3.5,{\\sigma }^{2})$ and $P(X<-2)=0.7257,$ find ${\\sigma }^{2}.$\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.5\\,$ | $\\,0.6915\\,$ | $\\,0.6950\\,$ | $\\,0.6985\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.6\\,$ | $\\,0.7257\\,$ | $\\,0.7291\\,$ | $\\,0.7324\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.7\\,$ | $\\,0.7580\\,$ | $\\,0.7611\\,$ | $\\,0.7642\\,$ |",
  "worked_solution": "First, we convert the given probability into a cumulative probability:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<-2)=0.7257\\,\u21d2\\,P(X\\le -2)=0.7257\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we transform to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le -2) & =0.7257 \\\\ P(Z\\le \\frac{-2+3.5}{\\sigma }) & =0.7257 \\\\ \u03a6(\\frac{1.5}{\\sigma }) & =0.7257 \\\\ \\frac{1.5}{\\sigma } & ={\u03a6}^{-1}(0.7257)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to the table, we have\n\n$$\n\u03a6(0.60)=0.7257\\,\u21d2\\,{\u03a6}^{-1}(0.7257)=0.60.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1.5}{\\sigma } & =0.60 \\\\ \\sigma  & =2.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2}={2.5}^{2}=6.25.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
